repository_artifacts:
Minimum tree:
`.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/feature.yml`, `bug.yml`, `config.yml` — real default-branch intake configuration only;
`.github/CODEOWNERS` — human owners for `.repo-os/**`, specs and workflows;
`.github/workflows/planning-validate.yml` — read-only deterministic schema/DoR checks;
`.github/workflows/project-reconcile.yml` — protected/default-branch invocation of the App, not untrusted issue code;
`.repo-os/project.schema.yaml` — logical project/field/option IDs and management mode, no GitHub node IDs;
`.repo-os/state-machine.yaml` — states, transitions, guards, actors and emitted events;
`.repo-os/dor.yaml` — applicable-by-type/risk predicates and named exception schema;
`.repo-os/risk-policy.yaml`, `capabilities.yaml`, `approval-policy.yaml` — risk floor, allowed tools/scopes, quorum/TTL/separation;
`.repo-os/schemas/{spec,plan-dag,readiness-token,event}.schema.json`;
`.repo-os/reconcile-policy.yaml` — authoritative fields, additive/destructive policy, scan interval and drift SLA;
`.repo-os/tests/fixtures/**` — transition, drift, webhook and hostile-input fixtures;
`planning/<issue-id>/spec.yaml`, `plan.yaml`, `acceptance.yaml` — protected revisioned artifacts (or immutable object records referenced by digest for high-volume repos);
`docs/planning-runbook.md`, `docs/adr/ADR-planning-control-plane.md`.

`spec.yaml` must hold problem, current/desired behavior, scope, non_goals, owners, risk flags, constraints, open questions, evidence refs, acceptance IDs, interfaces/migrations, permissions, rollout/rollback and expiry. `plan.yaml` is a DAG of stable task IDs with acceptance IDs, dependencies, expected paths/write set, budget, capability profile, stop rule and owner. Generated remote binding IDs and current item state belong in the runtime store/artifacts, not desired Git.
